WEBVTT

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.610
<i>I'm looking forward to seeing his reaction.</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.410
It's been a while, Gaston.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.510
How long <i>has</i> it been?

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.690
Ten years? Twenty?

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.270
It was back when you 
were still green, at least.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.840
Yeah, right.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.390
It was definitely back before 
your hands started to shake.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.620
So why'd you call me out here?

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.960
I can't imagine you got me 
here just to reminisce.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.540
Truth be told, I need to hire you.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.280
For a job? You trying to land 
a big score or something?

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.710
Not exactly.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:06.160
Plus, I'm retired now.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.760
Aw, quit making me so blue, Gaston.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.670
You're the guy everyone in the underworld 
used to call the "God of Forgery."

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.050
I need you to retrieve something for me...

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.770
Against the wishes of its owner, naturally.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.440
Easy as pie.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.140
You helped me when I was starting out,

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.680
so I'd dive headfirst into any 
fire or vault you asked me to.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.200
You sure you should be 
taking this so lightly?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.210
I'm asking you to go up against Mr. B.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.190
Oh, knowing that just makes me 
more dead set on doing it.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.110
I thought it might.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.200
How much time do you need?

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.950
Three days is plenty.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.700
Sounds great.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.710
We'll meet back here at the 
same time next week.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.440
Aw, come on. You don't trust my estimate?

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.370
Of course I trust you.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.210
And to prove it...

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.110
An advance payment.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.360
Is this...

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.850
Napoleon's Bible.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.670
An item from his traveling library.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.220
A replica?

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.730
I felt like stretching the old "art" muscles.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:22.480
When I pass away, 
read a prayer from it for me.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.000
<b>His Name is Albert</b>

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.630
Slow down a little, Mr. B.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.520
You don't understand.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.150
I've waited so long for this moment...

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.190
Then, another few minutes won't kill you.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.900
I'm going to take a shower.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.910
Good grief. Typical horny old man.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.400
The retinal capture looks good.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.920
Fingerprints, too.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:44.930
Fujiko!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.010
How long are you going to be in that shower?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.920
I can't wait much longer...

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.550
Oh...

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.220
Someone's a fan of the classics.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.230
Let's go.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.230
Retina and...

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.250
...fingerprints.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.790
I had to go through <i>a lot</i> to get these, y'know.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.060
Well, would you look at that?

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:21.670
Check it out. This little stash 
must be worth billions.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:25.060
I've seen tidier junkyards, to be honest.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:29.340
The guy throws cash at every piece 
he sees just so he can say he owns it.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.040
But once he has it, he loses interest.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.080
So he ends up hoarding 
all of it in a hole like this.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.850
It could be a masterpiece,

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.540
but once it's down here, it never 
sees the light of day again.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.570
Which is why...

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.340
The "b" in Mr. B stands for "black hole," huh?

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.200
Got it!

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:49.600
What's that?

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.850
A previously unknown Picasso 
that's never been on public display.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:59.590
Looks like something a kid doodled to me.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.810
You've got a sharp eye!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.600
You see, Gaston's grandkid drew that.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:09.100
Then, Gaston forged Picasso's 
signature on it as a joke...

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.220
And everyone thinks it's the real deal, huh?

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:15.300
All kinds of experts examined it, 
and all of them said it was legit.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.070
Just goes to show how good Gaston is.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.890
I guess when you're a master of your craft,

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.360
even a little prank can cause trouble.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.990
That goes for you, too.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.070
We're with the DGSE.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.600
We're joining this investigation.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.950
I see. So the Directorate-General 
for External Security is involved now...

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.990
<i>Director Guillaume probably sent them.</i>

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:58.210
Well, now we know who wanted it.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.720
<i>What should we do, Director?</i>

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.250
<i>This case is clearly a police matter.</i>

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.870
<i>An intelligence agency getting involved 
is overstepping their authority.</i>

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.100
Let them have their fun.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.360
The more pieces in play, 
the more exciting it gets.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.380
Talking shop so early 
in the morning, Albert?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:25.380
No... Just discussing the game.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.010
There's something weird 
about this painting.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.640
Weird? How?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.400
It looks way too much like a real Picasso.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.970
The composition makes it look like 
a piece from his <i>Las Meninas </i>series.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:44.740
Well, it's a forgery. Isn't it meant 
to look like a genuine Picasso?

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:45.900
Have you forgotten already?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:50.960
This painting was done by Gaston's grandkid. 
He just slapped Picasso's signature on it.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.330
The fact that it looks so much like 
a real work by Picasso is weird.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.260
Maybe it's just a coincidence.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.760
The smell's a little too strong for that.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:04.530
Are we talking about the stench of 
being saddled with a bad luck magnet?

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:08.400
More like the aroma of 
"a lie that was sold a little too hard."

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.860
What are you gonna do?

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:13.410
Hold your nose, pretend everything's 
hunky-dory, and just hand it over?

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.950
Guess I'll start digging...

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.290
Hey. How's business?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:29.310
What do you want, Lupin?

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:32.940
Looking to sell some of your 
collection? Hard up for cash?

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.170
Surely you jest.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.670
I <i>am </i>curious about this piece, though.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:42.190
You buy stuff that can't be 
sold legally, after all.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.050
Thought you might know something about it.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.960
It's trash. It doesn't have 
a shred of artistic value.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.930
The frame's probably worth more.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.310
Even with Picasso's signature on it?

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.320
I'm guessing by your reaction 
that you know what's up.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.440
Fine. Let's talk about this down below.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.470
Wh-Whoa! What is this?!

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:20.010
Degas, Monet, Delacroix...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.960
You've got a collection to rival Mr. B's.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.750
Please don't compare me to that 
artistically illiterate philistine.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.600
Doesn't stop you selling 
to him, though, does it?

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.820
That's just business.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.520
Incidentally, I was the one 
who sold this to Mr. B.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:37.810
You were?

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.610
At the request of Gaston.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.610
Say what?

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:46.720
He asked me to sell this 
painting to Mr. B years ago now.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:51.000
At first, I thought it was some stupid prank, 
but I soon realized the reason behind it.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:56.970
Any piece of art Mr. B buys 
never sees the light of day again.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.000
That makes his collection the 
perfect place to hide something.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.670
Understand?

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:04.000
Can't fault the logic...

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.380
But what if you need it back?

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:12.300
Mr. B never lets anything escape his grasp 
once he's got his hands on it, right?

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.560
True, except that Gaston 
has an old acquaintance...

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:19.000
that can even steal 
things from a black hole.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.200
Isn't that right?

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.490
We're being followed.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:47.250
Yep.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.830
You don't give up easy, do you?

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.890
Well, that didn't work!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.530
Guess I'll have to try harder to ditch him...

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.590
Hey, up here!

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.850
Don't move.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.730
Place the package on the 
ground by your feet.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.400
Slowly.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.950
Good. Now, put your hands above your—

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:24.610
Sneaking up from behind 
isn't usually my style.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.480
Good to know I can rely on you, partner!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.250
They're from the DGSE, huh? 
No wonder they were so persistent.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.890
Hey, Lupin. If these guys were watching 
Aghion's shop, that means...

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:45.610
They knew where he 
was getting his paintings.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.130
So they're after this thing, huh?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:48.760
Seems that way.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:53.190
What are you doing?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:58.490
I figured I'd ask a bigwig 
why they're after me.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.560
What is it?

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.310
<i>You're the head of the DGSE, I take it?</i>

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.230
Who the hell is this?!

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:15.250
<i>I'm the guy who has that 
thing you guys are after.</i>

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.330
Lupin?!

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.010
And to be frank,

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:21.340
I have a hard enough time playing 
hide-and-seek with Old Man Zenigata.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:23.870
So how about a trade?

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.700
Don't turn around.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.070
This is what you're after, right?

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:46.000
You mentioned a trade.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.400
What do you want? Money?

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:55.090
How about you enlighten me 
about something first?

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:58.670
Why are you so desperate 
to get your hands on this thing?

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.860
What's the point of asking that?

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.420
I'm a curious fella.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:07.330
Curiosity killed the rat, you know. 
Or wait, was it the cat?

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:08.800
Maybe it was the dog.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:18.030
Don't move!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.420
Aw, man.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:28.860
I didn't realize the DGSE 
had rented this place out.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.680
I said, don't move!

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.650
You're not using whatever 
you have in your hairpiece!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.290
Wow, you've got me all figured out, haven't you?

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.800
Well, at least let me 
say a prayer before I die.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:45.790
O Lord! Let there be light!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.810
Don't let him escape! Go!

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.600
I don't care if you have to kill him!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.100
So that's what you were after.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:31.790
Lupin?! How?

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.670
I don't mind being relied on,

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.930
but sometimes, I think he 
works me a little too hard.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.430
Let's save the questions for later.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.950
First, hand that to me.

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:59.380
Get a move on.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:01.480
Whoa, now.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:05.000
Peeling out isn't gonna throw 
off my aim, you know...

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:08.480
It'll just spray the roof with your brains.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:29.100
What's written in there? 
Places where you can find stashed loot?

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.780
Nothing as pleasant as that.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:34.880
Carnet noir–the black notebook.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.890
This thing holds the details of 
every misdeed and crime committed...

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:42.240
and covered up by 
the French police's top brass.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.540
Sounds like a godsend
 for internal affairs.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.300
If the stuff in here went public, forget 
the director general of the national police,

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.440
even the interior minister would be...

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:55.680
Must be one hell of a ticking time bomb
 from the perspective of the cops.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:59.740
Which is probably why their bosses have 
been trying to keep it firmly in the shadows.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.130
And yet, here it is in your hands.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.180
Yeah...

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:07.670
And why is Gaston mixed up in all this?

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:12.190
I'm a little early for our meeting, 
but I guess I should go talk to him.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.070
To Gaston, you mean?

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:17.640
I've been getting chased high 
and low because of this thing!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:21.140
Time to see what the old coot 
has to say for himself.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.340
Director, Lupin has left Paris.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.960
Uh, sir...

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.330
Don't worry.

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:40.100
He'll come to me in his own time.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.340
Hey, now.

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:48.350
You suddenly going all 
religious on me? What's up?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:53.100
I'm wondering why Gaston gave me this thing.

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:57.490
From the look on your face, 
I'm guessing only God knows.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.600
This place hasn't changed a bit...

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.510
...is something I wish I could say.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.220
It's actually pretty run-down now.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:18.000
Is Gaston's place nearby?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:21.550
Nah, if he's still in the 
same place, it's pretty far.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:34.640
A taxi?

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.020
What makes you think they come around 
here, where there's usually no fares?

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:38.900
Oof...

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:43.290
So much for that. I guess 
that means we'll be walking.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.800
Where are you headed, mister?

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.530
I want to see Gaston.

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:52.930
Not much chance of that, 
even if you do hike over there.

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.210
He's six feet under.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:02.540
Gaston died. A month ago.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:07.790
Don't be silly. I saw him just the other day...

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.310
"In the world of man, there is only 
one who is without falsehood...

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.680
...and that is the Lord," huh?

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.970
So who was the Gaston you met?

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.690
A ghost?

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:26.320
When I pass away, 
read a prayer from it for me.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:38.780
Albert...

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:42.250
Albert? Someone you know?

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.860
The last guy I ever wanted to see again.

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:18.800
Daisuke Jigen here.

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:22.770
This thing's like the Grim Reaper's notebook.

00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:25.410
It's been nothing but bad news since we got it.

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:30.330
They're even shooting rockets at us now.

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:35.540
Lupin, you oughta just toss 
that bad luck magnet.

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:37.660
Why do you care so much?

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Who Has the Black Notebook?</b>

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:41.280
Next time: Who Has the Black Notebook?

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:44.200
Lupin, just who is this "Albert" guy?
